<title>USA: US warns Japan against exporting out of recession.</title>
<headline>US warns Japan against exporting out of recession.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Trade Representative Charlene Barshefsky Friday warned Japan not to &quot;export its way&quot; out of recession.</p>
<p>&quot;I am concerned that Japan not think that it's going to export its way out of this recession, particularly with respect to significant increases in exports to the U.S.,&quot; Barshefsky told reporters when asked about Japan's trade deficit after speaking to a group of cattlemen.</p>
<p>The Commerce Department reported Thursday that the U.S. deficit with Japan edged up 0.7 percent to $4.29 billion in January.</p>
